  "signatureHoleDescription": "Hole 9 is the longest at Highland Park at 425 feet — a par 4 that ties together the course's wooded and open halves with a little elevation for good measure. It's the hole where a good drive earns a real birdie look, and the one that makes the round feel complete.",
